                <pb facs="0400" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">638.5131/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-02T17:00:00-05:00">November 2, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. Your 115, November 1, noon. Please consult Pixley and report by telegraph (1)
                    how much would acceptance of the plan reduce customs revenues on imports from
                    all gold basis countries and consequently to what extent require a reduction of
                    the budget; (2) is the French Government prepared to maintain equivalent to last
                    year’s coffee quota in exchange.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
